# Context Control Rules

## Objective
Keep the active context short while preserving long-term project memory.

## Required behavior

- after each major phase, write a summary to `context-control.md`
- include timestamp in every summary entry
- include progress, thoughts, suggestions, and supplementary notes
- compress temporary reasoning out of active context
- preserve only architecture, decisions, interfaces, and risks

## Trigger points

- after completing a command
- after finishing a milestone
- before switching to a different subsystem
- when context size becomes large

## Append-only rule

`context-control.md` must only be appended to.

## Extended reference (repo)

- Harness map and validator loop: `.cursor/harness/README.md`
- Entry shape and when to write: `.cursor/harness/context/entry-template.md`, `.cursor/harness/context/context-manager.md`
